{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792397962,"nonce":"nlZvSnZUyYLnU0AJqplfvK9DOi8=","title":"No map from a reference's source position to the symbol it resolves to","message":"TAST lowering resolves each identifier, field access, call and type reference to a SymbolId but keeps no record of where in the source that reference sits. With only declaration positions available, an IDE cannot answer anything about a *use* site: hover, go-to-definition, signature help at a call, find references, rename, document highlight or reference semantic tokens.\n\nNeeded: during expression and type lowering, record (file id, span) -\u003e SymbolId for every resolved reference, including field accesses on a typed receiver, static calls, enum constructors in patterns, type annotations, `new T()`, imports and `using`. Also record the expression's type, so hover on an arbitrary expression can show it.\n\nDepends on 72a3386418f58994afbee5392e994214cc2a8acf9db84f5bb8c60e19186dc48a.","files":null}]}